{
  "_comment": [
    "Generated by `hzl install` from etc/heinzel-settings.json.in.",
    "What the unattended agent may and may not do. The runner validates this",
    "file with `jq -e .` before every run and aborts if it is malformed,",
    "because `claude --print` silently ignores an invalid settings file -",
    "which would drop every rule below without a word.",
    "",
    "Three syntax rules, each of which was got wrong once and each of which",
    "fails silently rather than loudly. Do not 'tidy' them:",
    "",
    "  1. Path rules must name the Read or Edit tool. A path rule written for",
    "     Write, NotebookEdit or Glob is accepted and then never consulted.",
    "     Edit covers every built-in tool that changes a file, Write included.",
    "  2. An absolute path needs TWO leading slashes. A single slash anchors",
    "     at the settings file's own location, so /Users/you/x is a relative",
    "     path that matches nothing. Home-relative ~/x is fine as written.",
    "  3. Bash commands are matched in both the 'cmd *' and 'cmd:*' forms, so",
    "     the list does not depend on which pattern syntax is current.",
    "",
    "The worksheet is named in full in the allow list as well as being covered",
    "by the workdir's '/**' rule. Measured 2026-08-30: '/**' does reach a file",
    "in a dot directory, so the exact rule is redundant today. It stays because",
    "it makes the worksheet's permission independent of the workdir rule - the",
    "one line the run cannot proceed without should not depend on a glob that",
    "exists for a different reason and may be tightened later.",
    "",
    "The allow list ends with that pair of rules once per configured",
    "workspace, generated from DEFAULT_WORKDIR (the placeholder is a line of",
    "its own down there, and is replaced whole). A session may have several",
    "workspaces and",
    "one installed settings file serves all of them, so this allow list is",
    "wider than any single run needs: a run works in exactly one of them.",
    "That is deliberate and it is the sandbox that makes it acceptable - the",
    "sandbox roots at the run's own working directory, so the rules naming the",
    "other workspaces are inert for the whole of that run. The layer this does",
    "cost is the inner one: were the sandbox off, an agent could reach every",
    "configured workspace rather than one. Which is the argument for listing",
    "workspaces you are willing to have worked on unattended, and not every",
    "checkout on the disk.",
    "",
    "All three ledger files - the backlog, the blocked file and the completed",
    "archive - are denied by name, for the opposite reason: the agent works",
    "from a worksheet the runner merges back, so it has no business in the",
    "ledger, and 'the prompt told it not to' is not a control. One of the three",
    "is not enough: an agent that can edit the archive can mark its own work",
    "done, and one that can edit the blocked file can unblock the task it was",
    "told to leave alone. Keep the ledger outside the working directory as",
    "well - the sandbox is a path boundary, and that is what actually stops a",
    "subprocess reaching it.",
    "",
    "The sandbox is what actually confines the agent to the working directory.",
    "Permission rules govern Claude's own file tools; they do not govern a",
    "subprocess that opens a file itself, so a Python script could write",
    "anywhere without it. Measured: with the sandbox on but the permission",
    "mode left at auto, both the Write tool and a shell redirect still reached",
    "/tmp, because a command the sandbox refuses falls back to the ordinary",
    "permission flow and auto's classifier approves it. It takes the sandbox",
    "AND --permission-mode dontAsk together, which is why bin/hzl-run passes",
    "that mode. See docs/DESIGN.md section 4.5.",
    "",
    "Verify with docs/VERIFICATION.md phase 3a rather than trusting any of it.",
    "",
    "Self-improvement: the repository is writable, `etc/` is not. Heinzel works",
    "on its own source now, so a blanket denial of the repository would deny the",
    "point. The line is drawn at `etc/` because nothing in there is code - every",
    "file in it is control surface, and each one hands the agent a different way",
    "to widen its own boundary rather than do the task:",
    "",
    "  heinzel-settings.json      the deny list this file generates - editing it",
    "                             lifts the confinement directly",
    "  heinzel-settings.json.in   the same, one `hzl install` later",
    "  heinzel.conf               budget, schedule, workdir, engine, review",
    "  agent.plist.in             when the runner fires, and with what PATH",
    "  sudoers-{ticket,diag}.in   installed BY A HUMAN WITH sudo. An agent that",
    "                             writes these is writing a privileged file and",
    "                             waiting for someone to install it",
    "  pf-travel.conf.in          firewall rules, installed with privilege",
    "",
    "So `bin/`, `lib/`, `prompts/`, `docs/` and `tests/` are open and `etc/` is",
    "shut. Read stays allowed throughout - understanding the configuration is",
    "not the risk, changing it is. SECURITY.md records what this does and does",
    "not defend against; note in particular that `bin/hzl` is writable and a",
    "human later runs it with sudo, which is why review and the git history are",
    "load-bearing now rather than optional.",
    "",
    "Network: the sandbox proxies outbound traffic and refuses every domain",
    "not listed below (measured 2026-09-01: CONNECT tunnel 403). github.com is",
    "allowed deliberately so the agent can `git push origin` and push tags as",
    "the release ritual in docs/RELEASING.md requires. Everything else stays",
    "closed. The keychain write-back warning `failed to store: 100001` on push",
    "is expected inside the sandbox and harmless - the credential read works."
  ],
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": true,
    "network": {
      "allowedDomains": ["github.com"]
    }
  },
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Bash(sudo)", "Bash(sudo *)", "Bash(sudo:*)",
      "Bash(su)", "Bash(su *)", "Bash(su:*)",
      "Bash(doas)", "Bash(doas *)", "Bash(doas:*)",
      "Bash(pmset *)", "Bash(pmset:*)",
      "Bash(launchctl *)", "Bash(launchctl:*)",
      "Bash(systemsetup *)", "Bash(systemsetup:*)",
      "Bash(csrutil *)", "Bash(csrutil:*)",
      "Bash(spctl *)", "Bash(spctl:*)",
      "Bash(nvram *)", "Bash(nvram:*)",
      "Bash(dscl *)", "Bash(dscl:*)",
      "Bash(defaults write *)", "Bash(defaults write:*)",
      "Bash(crontab *)", "Bash(crontab:*)",
      "Bash(shutdown *)", "Bash(shutdown:*)",
      "Bash(reboot *)", "Bash(reboot:*)",
      "Bash(halt *)", "Bash(halt:*)",
      "Bash(diskutil *)", "Bash(diskutil:*)",
      "Bash(dd *)", "Bash(dd:*)",
      "Bash(git push --force*)", "Bash(git push -f*)",
      "Bash(git push --mirror*)", "Bash(git push --delete*)",
      "Bash(gh pr create *)", "Bash(gh pr create:*)",
      "Bash(gh pr merge *)", "Bash(gh pr merge:*)",
      "Bash(glab mr merge *)", "Bash(glab mr merge:*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf /*)", "Bash(rm -rf ~*)",

      "Read(~/.claude/settings.json)",
      "Read(~/.claude/.credentials.json)",
      "Read(~/.aws/**)",
      "Read(~/.ssh/**)",
      "Read(~/.gnupg/**)",
      "Read(~/.config/gcloud/**)",
      "Read(~/.kube/**)",
      "Read(~/.docker/config.json)",
      "Read(~/.netrc)",
      "Read(~/.git-credentials)",
      "Read(~/.npmrc)",
      "Read(~/.pypirc)",
      "Read(//**/.env)",
      "Read(//**/.env.*)",

      "Edit(__HEINZEL_HOME_ABS__/**)",
      "Edit(__HEINZEL_ROOT_ABS__/etc/**)",
      "Edit(~/.claude/**)",
      "Edit(~/Library/LaunchAgents/**)",

      "Read(__BACKLOG_ABS__)",
      "Edit(__BACKLOG_ABS__)",
      "Read(__BACKLOG_BLOCKED_ABS__)",
      "Edit(__BACKLOG_BLOCKED_ABS__)",
      "Read(__BACKLOG_COMPLETED_ABS__)",
      "Edit(__BACKLOG_COMPLETED_ABS__)"
    ],
    "allow": [
      "Bash(ls *)", "Bash(ls:*)",
      "Bash(git status *)", "Bash(git status:*)",
      "Bash(git diff *)", "Bash(git diff:*)",
      "Bash(git log *)", "Bash(git log:*)",
__WORKSPACE_RULES__
    ]
  }
}
